## 7. State Management

### Accessing State (MANDATORY)

```python
# CORRECT - Always use .get() with defaults
lead_id = state.get("lead_id", "unknown")
requirements = state.get("requirements", {})
missing_fields = state.get("missing_fields", [])
total_amount = state.get("total_amount", 0)
is_feasible = state.get("is_feasible", False)

# WRONG - Never access directly
lead_id = state["lead_id"]  # FORBIDDEN
```

### Handling Nested Requirements

```python
# Requirements may have nested structure from LLM
requirements = state.get("requirements", {})
nested_req = requirements.get("requirements", {}) if isinstance(requirements.get("requirements"), dict) else {}

# Check both levels
product_type = requirements.get("product_type") or nested_req.get("product_type") or "default"
quantity = requirements.get("quantity") or nested_req.get("quantity") or 0
```

### Returning State Updates

```python
# CORRECT - Return only changed fields
return {
    "status": FlowStatus.QUOTED,
    "total_amount": 1500.00,
    "current_node": "generate_quote",
}

# WRONG - Never return entire state
return state  # FORBIDDEN
```

